    "result_text": "Done. The full suite is green (71 tests, 0 failures) including the new `Cp59Tests`.\n\n## What the change required\n\nAll rejection responses (400, 409, 429) had to return an RFC7807 `application/problem+json` body with `type`, `title`, `status`, and `detail`. Investigating the escalation handlers showed almost all rejection paths already produced compliant `ProblemDetail` bodies via the shared `ProblemDetails.build(...)`:\n\n- **409** \u2014 `DuplicateIdentityExceptionHandler`, `CityAtCapacityExceptionHandler`\n- **429** \u2014 `DailyLimitExceptionHandler`\n- **400** \u2014 `ValidationExceptionHandler`\n\nThe one outlier was the **400 missing/invalid required-fields path** (`MissingFieldsExceptionHandler`), which returned a plain `FieldErrorsResponse` (`{\"errors\": [...]}`) as `application/json` \u2014 not RFC7807. That's exactly the path `Cp59Tests` exercises (POST an owner with `city` removed).\n\n## The fix\n\n- Rewrote `MissingFieldsExceptionHandler` to return `ResponseEntity<ProblemDetail>` built with `ProblemDetails.build(ex, BAD_REQUEST, ...)`, preserving the offending field names as an `errors` property on the problem body. Because the OfficeFloor\u2192Spring pipeline writes `ProblemDetail` through Spring's message converters, the response now carries the `application/problem+json` content type and the `status`/`type`/`title`/`detail` members automatically. HTTP status stays 400.\n- Deleted the now-unused `FieldErrorsResponse` record.\n\nVerified: `Cp59Tests` passes (asserts `application/problem+json` + `$.status == 400`), and no existing test regressed (no test depended on the old `errors`-only body shape).",
